SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] MaineCare in Education: Updated Joint Individ
 ual Education Program (IEP) Guidance for School Health-Related Services
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			MaineCare in Education: Updated Joint Individual Educat
 ion Program (IEP) Guidance for School Health-Related Services\nMaineCare i
 n Education: Updated Joint Individual Education Program (IEP) Guidance for
  School Health-Related Services\nOct 01\, 2026\nAs a reminder\, all provid
 ers who deliver services following the Individuals with Disabilities Educa
 tion Act (IDEA) must ensure all MaineCare-covered services are documented 
 following the Department of Health and Human Services/Maine Department of 
 Education Joint IEP Guidance document.\nThe Maine Department of Educat
 ion has released\nupdated Joint IEP Guidance\nto help schools follow feder
 al and state requirements. The updated guidance was developed through a co
 llaborative effort and is available on the\nMaineCare in Education web pag
 e\n.\nDOE first released the Joint Guidance on August 28\, 2026\, and has 
 re-issued this guidance effective September 18\, 2026. The reissued guidan
 ce replaces the previously issued Joint Guidance and provides clarificatio
 n in response to questions and feedback received from School Administrativ
 e Units (SAUs)\, providers\, and other interested parties.\nAll IEP docume
 nts must reflect the updated guidance as soon as possible\,\nbut no later 
 than thirty (30) days of the issuance of the guidance\n.\nProviders with c
 urrent prior authorizations for School Health-Related Services through Ace
 ntra should upload any updated documentation to Atrezzo. Acentra will acce
 pt IEP language from both versions through October 18\, 2026. Beginning Oc
 tober 19\, 2026\, Acentra will only accept IEP language from the new versi
 on re-issued on September 18\, 2026.\nFor technical assistance regarding t
 he billing and processing of MaineCare claims\, please contact your\nProvi
 der Relations Specialist\n.\nFor all other questions related to the provis
 ion of MaineCare School Health-Related Services\, please contact\nTrist\nh
 ttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-educa
 tion-updated-joint-individual-education-program-iep-guidance-school-health
 -3
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/mainecare-
 education-updated-joint-individual-education-program-iep-guidance-school-h
 ealth-3
