SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Veterans Forward Day - October 15
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, Maine veterans and their families have sacrificed 
 bravely for the United States of America and the State of Maine\, and it i
 s our duty to support those who have given so much for our country and com
 munities\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Veterans Forward\, a program of Easterseals Ma
 ine\, provides assistance to Maine veterans\, service members and their fa
 milies when other resources may not be available\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Vetera
 ns Forward helps veterans and their families with necessities such as hous
 ing\, substance use treatment\, home heating assistance\, food and clothin
 g\, and job training\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, on October 15\, 2026\, NewsRadio W
 GAN will host the “Make 12 Hours Count Radiothon” from 6:00 a.m. to 6:
 00 p.m. to raise awareness and funds to support Veterans Forward and the v
 eterans and military families it serves\;\nNOW\, THEREFORE\n\, be it resol
 ved that I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do hereby p
 roclaim October 15\, 2026 as\nVeterans Forward Day\nin Maine\, and I encou
 rage people across the state to support this important mission of serving 
 Maine veterans and their families.\nIn testimony whereof\, I have caused\n
 the Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto affixed GIVEN under my\nhand a
 t Augusta this twenty second day of\nSeptember Two Thousand Twenty-Six\nht
 tp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2026-09
 -veterans-forward-day-october-15
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-09-veterans-forward-day-october-15
